# IACT-AEP v1.0: Autonomous Engineering Interface Protocol

**Framework:** Integrative Associative Cognition Theory (IACT)  
**Architect / Author:** Hussain Salah (ޙުސައިން ޞަލާޙް)  
**Primary Objective:** Advancing Autonomous Engineering through Integrative Associative Cognition  

---

## 1. Overview & Attribution

The **Integrative Associative Cognition Theory (IACT)** is a conceptual and applied framework authored and developed by **Hussain Salah**. Its primary objective is to advance **Autonomous Engineering**—enabling machines, control protocols, and engineering systems to integrate real-time sensor telemetry, experiential memory, and cross-domain knowledge to make adaptive, safe, and autonomous decisions.

**IACT-AEP v1.0 (Autonomous Engineering Interface Protocol)** is the open, domain-agnostic protocol specification and reference implementation designed to operationalize IACT across autonomous vehicles, marine/aerial systems, robotics, and smart infrastructure.

---

## 2. 5-Layer Autonomous Engineering Control Stack

| Layer | Name | Operational Function |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Layer 1** | **SENSE** (`Sensory & Telemetry Ingestion`) | Standardizes multi-modal sensor streams, environmental telemetry, and context tags. |
| **Layer 2** | **RECALL** (`Experiential Memory Indexing`) | Retrieves relevant historical patterns and cross-domain engineering principles with context indexing. |
| **Layer 3** | **SYNTHESIZE** (`Associative Synthesis Engine`) | Combines live telemetry with recalled patterns to generate an adaptive control hypothesis (`synthesized_hypothesis`). |
| **Layer 4** | **GUARD** (`Validation & Safety Gate`) | Evaluates thermal, power, physical, and confidence thresholds (`safety_gate_passed`) before actuation. |
| **Layer 5** | **ACTUATE** (`Action & Execution Interface`) | Translates approved hypotheses into physical actuator commands or triggers fail-safe halt protocols. |

